      {
        "id": 199913,
        "name": "grysqrl",
        "username": "grysqrl",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/grysqrl/{size}/1909_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-07-08T17:17:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p><strong>Shadows Flicker Like Flame</strong> is a fear machine. All of its unique power cards generate fear. Higher levels of its innate power generate fear. It doesn't generate quite as much as Bringer of Dreams and Nightmares (especially in the late game, I've found), but it also doesn't have the limitation of not being able to damage/destroy the Invaders. Its innate power makes it pretty decent at dealing with explorers, pulling them out of lands before they build, but it isn't so strong against towns and cities. So, I would say that Shadows is largely about fear whereas Bringer of Dreams and Nightmares is exclusively about fear.</p><p>Comments on other spirits on your list:</p><ul>\n<li>\n<strong>Lightning's Swift Strike</strong> is really about building&nbsp;destruction. Raging Storm is good against clumps of explorers, but it doesn't really have any other ways to deal with them - most of its kit is about towns and cities.</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Heart of the Wildfire&nbsp;</strong>is about damage. Blight is a necessary side-effect, and it has limited ways to manage it, but I wouldn't say that blight is its focus.</li>\n<li>\n<strong>A Spread of Rampant Green</strong> is about&nbsp;slowing the invaders down. It is defensive in a different way than Vital Strength of the Earth is, expanding rapidly but then sacrificing itself to hamper the Invaders (vs Earth's direct Defense).</li>\n</ul>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:28:05.952Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
