      {
        "id": 199915,
        "name": "Bunston",
        "username": "Bunston",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bunston/{size}/1939_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-07-10T00:56:21.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"dpt\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dpt/48/1922_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> dpt:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>[…]Its ability to target any land with Dahan on the board can be extremely useful, if you remember to save up the Energy.[…]</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I would say this is Shadow's mechanical specialty. The 0 range powers tend to have a high strength to cost ratio, and the ability to use these from across the board is huge.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>I also think it's important to add that any spirit (with the exceptions of Bringer and Ocean) can eventually fill any role if you pick the right power cards. Don't get too caught up in sticking to your starting role.</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
